preConditionHook:
// EL: highestRange = Highest(high - low, lookback), with
//     high - low >= highestRange.
//
// Highest bottoms out in Extremes, which is EasyLanguage SOURCE: seeded at
// bar 0, scanning bars 1..Length-1, strict comparison so a tie keeps the
// earliest bar. Being EL source it carries the relational tolerance, so the
// scan uses el_gt rather than > -- the same expansion Breakout writes.
//
// The window INCLUDES the current bar, so the range can never exceed the
// maximum and the test is a rank against it: >= is true exactly on the bar
// that ties the window maximum, which is why Breakout's EL `=` becomes a
// tolerance-carrying inequality here rather than a float equality.
//
// The Highest argument is a price EXPRESSION with real history, not an EL
// variable, so there is no zero-filled warm-up mirror to build.
// Direction-agnostic: both sides are identical text.
// Both scratch locals are class members and persist across bars, so they are
// reassigned unconditionally every bar.
barRange = high[0] - low[0];
highestRange = barRange;
for (int i = 1; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i] - low[i], highestRange)) highestRange = high[i] - low[i];
}
